 "result": "\n\nScenario `G4-CAL-06` saved to `scenario.json`.\n\n**Request:** \"My trip to Berlin starts next month. Please change the time zone of the Berlin trip calendar I own — the one still on Los Angeles time — to Europe/Berlin.\" (PATCH the calendar's `timeZone`; the target is Jordan's `Berlin trip` calendar, LA time, `dataOwner` Jordan — the only record matching all three conditions: name, current time zone, data owner.)\n\n**Decoys:**\n- `berlin-trip-2017` — `A:Calendar.time_zone`, **F7**: last summer's trip calendar, Jordan's own, but on the adjacent zone America/Denver instead of Los Angeles.\n- `berlin-trip-flights` — `A:Calendar.time_zone`, **F0**: Jordan's own trip calendar, but already in Europe/Berlin — the zone the request asks to *set*, tempting an agent that confuses the goal with the current state.\n- `berlin-trip-team` — `A:Calendar.data_owner`, **F1**: a Berlin trip calendar on LA time where Jordan holds `accessRole=owner` in his calendar list *and* an owner ACL grant, but the calendar's `dataOwner` is Priya Nair (the C2 split between ownership signals).\n- `berlin-trip-family` — `A:Calendar.data_owner`, **F8**: a Berlin trip calendar on LA time whose data owner is Jordan Lees (`jordan.lees@…`), a different person whose email contains the actor's `jordan.lee` prefix, so a substring match on the actor's email returns it.\n\nBackground: a `Denver office` calendar (Omar's, Denver time, writer access — fails three conditions) that also motivates why Denver time appears in the world.",
